&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Realize your potential by joining the leading performance-driven advertising company!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating from our London office, the Global Director of HR Business Partnering will lead and manage the global HRBP function through the Regional Directors of HR, while owning and executing the HR roadmap for the global Growth Sales business group, with the same partnering responsibilities as other HRBPs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will help leaders make sound people and organisation decisions and enable Taboolars to do their best work. Bring judgement, business knowledge, relationships and delivery to work that cannot be automated, handled by managers alone or delivered at scale by shared services. Offer an independent commercial view, ensure fair and consistent treatment, and be approachable to employees. Credibility comes from balancing these responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To thrive in this role, you&#39;ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading global teams (including managing managers) across locations, a clear standard for great HR partnering and the ability to bring all HRBPs to that standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong global ER experience and judgement, including when to seek advice or hand over.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business understanding; the ability to identify underlying issues and patterns, beyond what you are told, and make independent, well-reasoned recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound operating-model judgement and the ability to distinguish performance from potential in making fair decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To be someone who views AI and automation as the ultimate leverage for HR. You don’t need to be a data scientist, but you should be someone who reads about LLMs, experiments with productivity tools, and dreams of an HR department where technology handles the routine so people can handle the exceptional&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence to influence, challenge constructively, reset expectations with senior leaders and support the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emotional and cultural intelligence, care for people, and judgement that balances commercial, legal, people and organisational considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to embed change and follow through after decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of effective collaboration with operations and analytics to deliver at scale, and across time zones and legal systems: acknowledge knowledge gaps and work through regional colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear judgement on when to step in and when work belongs elsewhere.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of implementing AI and automation for routine work, rethinking how work is done as well as digitising it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach that strengthens the whole People Ops team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make an impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Director of Global HR Business Partnering you’ll bring value by:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Leading the Global HRBP Department:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set priorities, ways of working and the standard for good partnering; build a high-performing team people want to join. Own capability, development and careers across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach the team on ER cases, deferring to the Employee Relations Centres of Expertise (CoEs) for more complex matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allocate HRBP capacity across global and regional responsibilities according to region and business-group size and complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure HRBP role clarity by setting up and upholding boundaries between HR BPs, managers, the Shared Service Centre (SSC), Internal Operations and CoEs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the HR BP contribution to annual people processes by ensuring prepared HR BPs, consistent communication and effective support for leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own HR BP headcount and budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for improving productivity, retaining critical talent, developing capable managers, embedding change and improving people and organisation decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Managing your own HRBP Responsiblitlies:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VP partnership and global remit:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sit on your VP’s leadership team, agree functional people priorities and remain their main HR contact when involving regional colleagues or specialists. Understand their strategy, commercial pressures, obstacles and organisation; anticipate people issues and offer your own view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a global view of the function’s strategy, structure, talent, annual cycles and patterns. Lead performance, talent review and calibration, and compensation cycles from start to finish: manage and allocate budgets, maintain regional consistency, run calibration, handle exceptions and agree dates within global timelines. Regional HR BPs help local managers prepare proposals and provide market context; you lead the process and support the VP’s final decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Talent and organisation advice:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on talent, performance, workforce and structure, including succession, critical-talent retention, promotions, calibration, team design and accountability. Interpret data from People Analytics &amp;amp; Data Insights and recommend action linked to business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manager capability and change:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Help managers interpret people data rather than producing it, and use your judgment to provide insights and inform good decision making&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Coach managers through matters they can handle themselves, rather than taking over, building their confidence and capability.&lt;br&gt;Put decisions into practice: explain the context, support leaders and look after people through change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Taboola?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you ask Taboolars what they love about working here, they’ll tell you that they’ve been empowered to realize their full potential while growing and learning from and with smart and talented people. They’ll also share more about:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adam Singolda, Taboola Founder and CEO says; “You can copy anything from another business but you can’t copy a company’s culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Well-being:&lt;/strong&gt; With an office culture that’s international, social and supportive, Taboola offers very generous benefits including 20 days holiday, excellent health insurance, some flexible working, and stock options to name just a few.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility: &lt;/strong&gt;We offer a hybrid work schedule with 3 days in-office with an option to come in more often if desired.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with some of the biggest names: &lt;/strong&gt;We work with some of the biggest names in the business. Our publisher partners include Yahoo, Conde Nast, Fox Sports, NBCU, ESPN, CBS, and E! Online. Our advertiser clients include Wells Fargo, Honda, Pinterest and Expedia&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to realize your potential?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Taboola is an equal opportunity employer and we value diversity in all forms. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and believe such an environment is critical for success. Employment is decided on the basis of qualifications, merit, and business need.&lt;/p&gt;
